# Cloudflare Worker local secrets/config (gitignored real file: .dev.vars)
# Copy to .dev.vars only if you need to override base wrangler.jsonc local vars.
# Never put production values, service-role keys, or DB passwords here.
#
# Optional POC routing override. Base local config defaults to the public Valhalla demo:
# VALHALLA_BASE_URL=https://valhalla1.openstreetmap.de
#
# Point at self-hosted Valhalla when available, e.g.:
# VALHALLA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8002
#
# Optional non-secret provider base URLs (defaults exist in wrangler.jsonc):
# OPEN_METEO_BASE_URL=https://api.open-meteo.com
# TOMTOM_BASE_URL=https://api.tomtom.com
#
# Optional TomTom Traffic API key (local secret only). Required only when motor-traffic
# enrichment is enabled in the planner. Ordinary CI and traffic-disabled runs do not need it.
# Obtain a key from https://developer.tomtom.com/ and enable the Traffic API product on that key.
# A key without Traffic API access returns HTTP 401/403 on flowSegmentData calls.
# Never commit the real value.
# TOMTOM_API_KEY=replace-with-local-tomtom-key
